  "worked_solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\frac{2x{y}^{2}-1}{{x}^{2}y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot {x}^{2}y-(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}({x}^{2}y)}{({x}^{2}y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{y}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}y-(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot 2xy}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}{y}^{3}-4{x}^{2}{y}^{3}+2xy}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy-2{x}^{2}{y}^{3}}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy(1-x{y}^{2})}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-x{y}^{2})}{{x}^{3}y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=1-x{y}^{2}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
